answer:
Use {}. Example:
local t = {}
local playerInfo = {}

Use setmetatable(tbl, metatable). Example:
local mt = {__index = function(t, k) return "missing" end}
setmetatable(myTable, mt)

Use __index in the metatable to return fallback values or proxy table keys. Example:
local defaults = {speed = 250}
setmetatable(playerData, {__index = defaults})

Define __add in the metatable. Example:
local mt = {__add = function(a, b) return a.x + b.x end}
setmetatable(vec1, mt)

Define __tostring in the metatable. Example:
local mt = {__tostring = function(v) return v.name end}
setmetatable(obj, mt)

Define __newindex to intercept writes. Example:
local proxy = {}
setmetatable(proxy, {__newindex = function(t, k, v) error("Cannot assign") end})
